#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101819} :activity/id #uuid "eca39ae6-43d5-5733-a009-55c6a59593e6" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048856 :topic/id #uuid "c6b5949b-df61-5d36-8c55-055311c70a59" :topic/math-academy-id 1176} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101819 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186102012 :tutorial/content "Let's see a trick that can be used to compute the sum of the following series:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n = 1}^\\infty \\dfrac 1 {n (n + 1)}\n$$\n\nFirst, we can use partial fractions to write\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{n(n+1)} = \\dfrac{1}{n} - \\dfrac{1}{n+1}\n$$\n\nThen the sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n = 1}^\\infty \\dfrac 1 {n (n + 1)} = \\sum_{n = 1}^\\infty\\left(\\dfrac{1}{n} - \\dfrac{1}{n+1}\\right)\n$$\n\nComputing the first few partial sums, *without* simplifying, notice that many terms cancel:\n\n$\\require{cancel}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ns_{1} &= (1- \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\\ns_{2} &= (1 - \\frac{1}{2}) + (\\frac{1}{2}- \\frac{1}{3}) \\\\\ns_{3} &= (1 - \\frac{1}{2}) + (\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3}) + (\\frac{1}{3}- \\frac{1}{4}) \\\\\ns_{4} &= (1 - \\frac{1}{2}) + (\\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3}) + (\\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{1}{4}) + (\\frac{1}{4}- \\frac{1}{5})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor each partial sum, we always end up canceling all terms except for the first and last terms. We say that this infinite series is a **telescoping series**, meaning that it consists of only a finite number of terms after canceling.\n\nSo, if $s_N$ is the $N$th partial sum of the series, we have\n\n$$\ns_N = {\\color{blue}{1}} {\\color{red}{\\,-\\, \\dfrac 1 {N + 1}}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can determine the sum of the series by computing the limit of $s_N$ as $N\\to\\infty$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(n = 1)^(∞)(1)/(n(n + 1)) &= lim_(N → ∞)(1 - \\frac{1}{N + 1}) \\\\\n&= 1 - 0 \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "7785a1f9-f6fd-5dac-bbab-9da2b149e341" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6768 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "f09ad925-45f1-583f-9d96-f7db4c4c6d03" :step/math-academy-id 41059 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101820}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101820 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100965 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100583 :question/id #uuid "f2af7002-adda-5491-9747-11672a1e47e5" :question/math-academy-id "e-10834"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8b8750bd-210d-5da2-aeb2-83fd615d979d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050050} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050706}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101491} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101492}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Series Whose Denominator Is the Product of N and N+1"} :step/id #uuid "1d7a95a6-44a2-55cb-a4bc-c0ee15b8cece" :step/math-academy-id 41060 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101821}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101821 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100966 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100584 :question/id #uuid "278de328-de74-51ef-a6e6-380a99dbcd95" :question/math-academy-id "e-10835"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c034fbc0-b497-53f2-8e9c-9d12afa04ec2" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101219} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101457} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101458}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum of a Series Whose Denominator Is the Product of Two Consecutive Expressions"} :step/id #uuid "053b72df-f735-53b4-9d30-87093c9b677a" :step/math-academy-id 41063 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101822}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101822 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100967 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100585 :question/id #uuid "36d7c5e4-2d11-55cd-98da-3f9d43d46125" :question/math-academy-id "e-10836"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f1114c-8155-5578-8e1d-0ba8fc010157" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101546} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101547} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101548}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating t